From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:23:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the rollout trace tests from failing on a slow
 app-server start

The success and stream-failure test started a new `codex app-server` four times in
one test, each limited to the 10 second request wait, so one slow start under runner
load failed the whole test. When initialization hit that wait, the early error return
dropped the mock server, whose unmet-expectation panic replaced the real
"deadline has elapsed" error.

- The four cases are separate tests that share one helper.
- TestAppServerBuilder::with_request_timeout replaces the response wait for one
  server; the default stays 10 seconds (25 on Windows). Both rollout trace tests use
  it with 60 seconds, so the wait only catches a hang.
- The helper uses the mock server without an expectation and checks that exactly one
  responses request arrived after the other assertions, so an earlier error is the
  one reported.
